{"reference":"2 Samuel 3","book":"2 Samuel","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Book’s Movement","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Second Samuel begins with David’s accession and the consolidation of his kingdom. This chapter belongs to that opening movement, while the book later turns to the ark, the dynasty promise, royal abuse, household violence, rebellion, grief, and a closing appendix.","verse_refs":["2 Samuel 1","2 Samuel 10:1-19","2 Samuel 11:1-27","2 Samuel 12:1-31","2 Samuel 13:1-39","2 Samuel 14:1-33","2 Samuel 15:1-37","2 Samuel 16:1-23","2 Samuel 17:1-29","2 Samuel 18:1-33","2 Samuel 19:1-43","2 Samuel 20:1-26","2 Samuel 21:1-22","2 Samuel 22:1-51","2 Samuel 23:1-39","2 Samuel 24:1-25","2 Samuel 2:1-32","2 Samuel 4:1-12","2 Samuel 5:1-25","2 Samuel 6:1-23","2 Samuel 7:1-29","2 Samuel 8:1-18","2 Samuel 9:1-13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_samuel_003_ab3787c8d0b85362e3a17a61"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}